@startuml
title Escape Room Adventure | Automatic acquisition and fresh two-gate output
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam participantPadding 8
autonumber
actor Player
participant GameView as View
participant GameController as Controller
participant "Focused Interactor\nthrough its InputBoundary" as UC
participant Game
participant "current Room" as Room
participant "destination Room" as NextRoom
participant Inventory
participant "Room.doorLock\nItemLock" as Door
participant "Room.exitChallenge\nTriviaLock" as Quiz
participant "TriviaDataAccessInterface\nHTTP adapter" as API
participant GamePresenter as Presenter
participant GameViewModel as Model
participant GameOutputAssembler as Assembler

note over Player, Model
  ItemLock and exit Trivia may finish in either order. There are seven use cases.
  Every success, error and changed=false result produces fresh immutable output.
  Each response renders before the next depicted input. Missing Game uses
  fromNoGame(message) and the same presenter -> EDT model -> View completion.
  Commands use one serial worker. Getters, output assembly and rendering never acquire items.
  Presenter constructs ViewState inside its EDT callback, preserving CURRENT busy.
  finally queues an EDT completion AFTER output; it clears UI busy + admission guard together.
  Another command is admitted only after that result render/completion.
end note

group new game: starting visible items are acquired before its first output
  Player -> View : choose a story
  View -> Controller : start(templateId)
  Controller -> UC : StartGameInputBoundary.start(templateId)
  ref over UC, Inventory
    Load template through the story port; GameFactory.create constructs a candidate.
    Its new-game constructor invokes private enterRoom(startingRoomId) before publication:
    resolve room, obtain visibleCollectables IDs, preflight ALL transfers, then enter/acquire.
    The same original items become revealed INVENTORY items; no duplicate instances.
    Future-room visible items stay in ROOM until normal entry.
  end ref
  alt candidate is valid
    UC -> UC : context.replace(candidate); initial message names\ncandidate.inventoryItems() once
  else template or creation fails
    UC -> UC : keep previous context; message=error
  end
  UC -> Assembler : fromGame(currentGame, message, Optional.empty())\nor fromNoGame(message)
  Assembler --> UC : fresh output; new-game message includes its initial obtained names
  UC -> Presenter : present(output)
  Presenter -> Model : setState(viewState), via UiDispatcher on EDT
  Model --> View : notify -> render(model.getState())
end

group interaction: automatic appearance, failed input or repeated item IDs
  Player -> View : choose an object action
  View -> Controller : interact(objectId, actionId, optionalItemId)
  Controller -> UC : InteractInputBoundary.execute(...)
  UC -> Game : interact(objectId, actionId, optionalItemId)
  Game -> Game : validate ACTIVE, current object/action and one-shot completion
  alt invalid access OR completed one-shot
    Game -> Game : unchanged error/no-op; no newly obtained items
  else uncompleted or legitimate repeatable action
    opt an itemId was supplied
      Game -> Inventory : require(optionalItemId)
      Inventory --> Game : actual held item, or precondition failure
    end
    alt supplied item is not actually held
      Game -> Game : unchanged item-precondition error
    else supplied item resolved, or no item supplied
      Game -> Room : prepareInteraction(objectId, actionId, heldItem)
      alt item, condition or state-effect validation fails
        Room --> Game : DomainException; no mutation
      else preparation succeeds
        Room --> Game : ActionPlan with effects + appearingItemIds
        Game -> Game : preflightAcquisition(room, plan.appearingItemIds)
        note over Game, Inventory
          For EACH appearance ID, skip it if already in inventory.
          Otherwise require the remaining local ROOM item.
          Validate ALL IDs before any object effect, completion or location mutation.
          Authored appearingItemIds refer to original items of this action's own room.
        end note
        alt any new appearance target is invalid
          Game -> Game : preserve object state, completion and every item location
        else every acquisition is prevalidated
          Game -> Room : applyInteraction(plan)
          Room -> Room : apply object-state effects; record nonrepeatable completion
          Game -> Game : acquireItems(room, plan.appearingItemIds)
          loop each appearance ID not already in inventory
            Game -> Room : takeCollectable(itemId), already prevalidated
            Room --> Game : the same Collectable
            Game -> Game : mark this item revealed
            Game -> Inventory : add(the same item)
          end
          Game -> Game : newItems = ONLY actual new transfers;\nappend their labels to resultText
          note over Room, Inventory
            Repeated IDs yield no duplicate and no second Obtained notice.
            Other valid repeatable state effects may still change the room.
            State effects never transfer items or unlock either gate.
          end note
        end
      end
    end
  end
  Game --> UC : DomainResult(code, changed, resultText) or DomainException
  UC -> Assembler : fromGame(game, resultText/error, Optional.empty())
  Assembler --> UC : fresh inventory, action text + actual obtained names, gates and movement flags
  UC -> Presenter : present(output), including errors and no-ops
  Presenter -> Model : setState(viewState), via UiDispatcher on EDT
  Model --> View : notify -> render(model.getState())
end

group ItemLock attempt checks the complete inventory
  Player -> View : choose Attempt door
  View -> Controller : useItems(doorLockId)
  Controller -> UC : UseItemInputBoundary.execute(doorLockId)
  UC -> Game : useItems(doorLockId)
  Game -> Game : validate ACTIVE and current Room.doorLock ID
  alt invalid status or target
    Game -> Game : unchanged error
  else current active door
    Game -> Door : isUnlocked()
    alt already unlocked
      Door --> Game : true
      Game -> Game : unchanged result BEFORE any item checks
    else still locked
      Door --> Game : false
      Game -> Door : tryUnlock(inventory)
      Door -> Inventory : containsAll(requiredItemIds)
      alt any exact required ID missing
        Inventory --> Door : false
        Door --> Game : unchanged result with missing-item text
        note over Inventory, Door
          Required={brassKey,note}; held={coin,rope}.
          Equal counts with wrong IDs still fail.
        end note
      else every required ID held
        Inventory --> Door : true
        Door -> Door : unlocked = true
        Door --> Game : successful unlock result
      end
    end
  end
  note over Inventory, Door : Door checks leave every item held.
  Game --> UC : DomainResult or DomainException
  UC -> Assembler : fromGame(game, resultText/error, Optional.empty())
  Assembler -> Game : itemDetails(currentRoom.doorLock.requiredItemIds())
  Game --> Assembler : read-only metadata across rooms + inventory
  Assembler --> UC : fresh required names, held IDs, canUnlock, gates and canMove/finalRoom
  UC -> Presenter : present(output)
  Presenter -> Model : setState(viewState), via UiDispatcher on EDT
  Model --> View : notify -> render(model.getState())
end

group Trivia.open: cached, fetched, API failure or invalid target
  Player -> View : choose exit Trivia
  View -> Controller : openTrivia(exitTriviaId)
  Controller -> UC : TriviaInputBoundary.open(exitTriviaId)
  UC -> Game : triviaFor(exitTriviaId)
  alt domain query rejects the target/status
    Game --> UC : DomainException
    UC -> UC : message=error; activeLockId=empty
  else accessible current-room exitChallenge
    Game -> Quiz : getTrivia()
    Quiz --> Game : cached question or empty
    Game --> UC : cached question or empty
    alt initialized question exists
      UC -> UC : reuse it; activeLockId=exitTriviaId
    else API question is uninitialized
      UC -> Game : triviaSpecFor(exitTriviaId)
      Game --> UC : spec
      UC -> API : fetchQuestion(spec)
      alt API failure
        API --> UC : DataAccessException
        UC -> UC : message=retry error; activeLockId=empty
        note over Game, Quiz : Question and gate remain unchanged; opening may be retried.
      else API success
        API --> UC : Trivia
        UC -> Game : installTrivia(exitTriviaId, trivia)
        Game -> Quiz : initializeTrivia(trivia), once
        UC -> UC : activeLockId=exitTriviaId
      end
    end
  end
  UC -> Assembler : fromGame(game, message, activeLockId)
  Assembler --> UC : fresh output; activeTrivia only for valid initialized question
  UC -> Presenter : present(output), including API-error output
  Presenter -> Model : setState(viewState), via UiDispatcher on EDT
  Model --> View : notify -> render(model.getState())
end

group Trivia.submit: correct, wrong, uninitialized or repeated answer
  Player -> View : submit answer (or direct uninitialized input)
  View -> Controller : submitAnswer(exitTriviaId, answer)
  Controller -> UC : TriviaInputBoundary.submit(exitTriviaId, answer)
  UC -> Game : submitAnswer(exitTriviaId, answer)
  Game -> Game : validate ACTIVE and current Room.exitChallenge ID
  alt invalid status or target
    Game -> Game : unchanged error
  else valid active target
    Game -> Quiz : submitAnswer(answer)
    alt already passed
      Quiz --> Game : unchanged result BEFORE answer checks
    else question is uninitialized
      Quiz --> Game : uninitialized-question error; unchanged
    else wrong answer
      Quiz --> Game : wrong-answer result; unchanged; same cached question
    else correct answer
      Quiz -> Quiz : markUnlocked()
      Quiz --> Game : changed=true; success result
    end
  end
  Game --> UC : DomainResult or DomainException
  note over UC, API : Submit NEVER calls API. An uninitialized attempt changes no question/gate state.
  UC -> UC : activeLockId=exitTriviaId only for wrong answer to initialized question;\notherwise empty
  UC -> Assembler : fromGame(game, resultText/error, activeLockId)
  Assembler -> Game : canMove()
  Game --> Assembler : ACTIVE AND current Room.canLeave()
  Assembler --> UC : fresh gate/movement flags; wrong answer retains the same active prompt
  UC -> Presenter : present(output), for EVERY answer outcome
  Presenter -> Model : setState(viewState), via UiDispatcher on EDT
  Model --> View : notify -> render(model.getState())
  note over View, Model : Correct completion of the second gate enables movement in this refreshed view.
end

group movement: enter/acquire atomically, escape or remain blocked
  note over Player, View
    Label = finalRoom ? Escape : Next room; enabled by canMove.
    No destination selector or successor ID enters UI output.
  end note
  Player -> View : choose Next room / Escape (or direct blocked command)
  View -> Controller : move()
  Controller -> UC : MoveInputBoundary.execute()
  UC -> Game : move()
  Game -> Game : check ACTIVE
  alt inactive
    Game -> Game : unchanged status error
  else ACTIVE
    Game -> Room : canLeave()
    Room -> Door : isUnlocked()
    Room -> Quiz : isUnlocked()
    alt door unlocked AND exit Trivia passed
      Room --> Game : true
      Game -> Room : nextRoomId()
      Room --> Game : Optional successor ID
      alt successor present
        Game -> Game : enterRoom(nextRoomId): resolve destination
        alt destination reference invalid
          Game -> Game : preserve room/inventory; error
        else destination exists
          Game -> NextRoom : visibleCollectables()
          NextRoom --> Game : visible Collectables
          Game -> Game : visibleIds = IDs of the returned items
          Game -> Game : preflightAcquisition(destination, visibleIds)
          alt any transfer is invalid
            Game -> Game : preserve current room and ALL item locations
          else all transfers are prevalidated
            Game -> Game : currentRoomId = successor ID
            Game -> Game : acquireItems(destination, visibleIds)
            loop each visible ID not already held
              Game -> NextRoom : takeCollectable(itemId)
              NextRoom --> Game : the same Collectable
              Game -> Game : mark it revealed
              Game -> Inventory : add(the same item)
            end
            Game -> Game : resultText includes ONLY newly obtained labels
          end
        end
      else successor empty (Room.isFinal())
        Game -> Game : status = ESCAPED; no extra item acquisition
      end
    else either gate incomplete
      Room --> Game : false
      Game -> Game : preserve room/status; explain missing gate
    end
  end
  Game --> UC : DomainResult or DomainException
  UC -> Assembler : fromGame(game, resultText/error, Optional.empty())
  Assembler -> Game : canMove()
  Game --> Assembler : ACTIVE AND current Room.canLeave()
  Assembler -> Game : currentRoom()
  Game --> Assembler : POST-COMMAND current Room
  Assembler -> Assembler : finalRoom = returnedRoom.isFinal()
  Assembler --> UC : fresh inventory/message with canMove + finalRoom
  UC -> Presenter : present(output), for success AND blocked/error outcomes
  Presenter -> Model : setState(viewState), via UiDispatcher on EDT
  Model --> View : notify -> render(model.getState())
end

ref over Player, Model
  Save/load retains schema 4 and the existing predecessor-gates validation.
  Compatible immutable template versions define successors and appearance-item rules.
  Restore uses state construction, never enterRoom/acquireItems; it replays no action or acquisition.
  Load and later refresh display existing inventory without another Obtained notice.
  No acquisition ledger or additional output field is introduced.
  Detailed save/load success/error response cycles: escape-room-save-sequence.puml.
end ref
@enduml
